name o2-01-vector-1
timeout 400
time 1984-06-14T06:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN O2, SORTIE 1 OF 10 - PVO INTERCEPT EXERCISE: GROUND CONTROL IN ITS PURE FORM.
# THIS FILE IS THE CAMPAIGN'S BASELINE. Sorties 02, 03, 04 and 05 are this file with exactly ONE
# declared change each, and each of them names this file as its control.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/o2-pvo-intercept.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: none - it IS the control, of o2-02, o2-03, o2-04 and o2-05.
#
# THE ANCHOR IS A DOCTRINE PLUS A PIECE OF HARDWARE, NOT A BATTLE, and that is declared rather than
# dressed up. THE DOCTRINE HALF WAS RAISED TO [T1] IN THIS ROUND: the two CIA reading-room
# translations the spec listed as IDENTIFIED AND UNREAD were retrieved and read, and the campaign
# file's Knowledge 1 now carries them. The hardware half is the MiG-29's own guidance panel, which
# both DCS manuals document as NOT IMPLEMENTED - so what FlightBox flies is the documented
# SUBSTITUTE loop: voice BRAA -> the pilot TYPES three entries -> the scan volume is aimed -> and
# only then does the radar exist at all.
#
# THE ARENA, and every coordinate in it is [SET]. An exercise has no battlefield, so this campaign flies
# over the Soviet air-defence firing range at Ashuluk, Astrakhan oblast [T4], taken as ~47.30 N 47.90 E
# and NOT improved on. Flown under `--elev const` on a 0 m datum and with NO TERRAIN MASKING (gap C4).
#   the defended complex   a command post (target_hard) and a vehicle park (target_soft) - the objects
#                          the vector exists to protect
#   the early-warning set  a P-18, `set emcon free`, deployed forward of the complex on the approach
#                          axis. GAP C1 IS CLOSED AND THIS CAMPAIGN RE-CHECKED IT: the spec still says
#                          "target_soft only, the EW radar that generates the vector is inert". It is
#                          not inert any more - it radiates, it is heard by the intruder's RWR as
#                          `kind=surface-search` from t = 0.1, it builds its own tracks, and it can be
#                          killed. Every ground object in this campaign is OURS and none is a target
# Scale at this latitude: 1 deg of longitude = 75 490 m, 1 deg of latitude = 111 132 m [DERIVED].
#
# TEMPORAL HONESTY AND ITS DIRECTION. The PVO's own subject was a large, slow, high, unmanoeuvring
# aircraft - a bomber or an ELINT platform - and FlightBox has neither as a flyable module (gap C7: the
# catalogue's `tu95` row is a KINEMATIC MOVER, not an airframe). The intruder here is an F-16: faster,
# smaller and far harder to find than the aircraft the doctrine was written against. THE SUBSTITUTION
# MAKES THE INTERCEPT HARDER THAN HISTORY, so a FlightBox result in which the loop still closes says
# something WEAKER than the doctrine claimed, and one in which it does not close says nothing about it.
#
# AND THE CATALOGUE IS NOT A WAY ROUND IT. Four `air` rows are ACCEPTED, and ACCEPTED in
# doc/modules/air/flight-model-recipe.md means ACCEPTED AS A FLIGHT MODEL - the promotion gate measures
# the DECK and nothing else. It measures no weapon, no sensor and no engagement, and four of the ten
# armed rows cannot employ anything at all. A campaign citing a catalogue row as a COMBATANT would be
# citing something no gate has ever checked, so this campaign cites none: every aircraft in all ten
# files is one of the two flyable modules.
#
# THE STRUCTURAL DISCLOSURE, repeated in all ten files because a reader who skips it reads every result
# backwards:
#   1. THE CONTROLLER IS A STRING (gap C6). `set brief_gci` is fixed before the run: nothing re-vectors,
#      nothing goes silent mid-intercept, nothing is wrong halfway through. Every wrong brief in this
#      campaign is wrong FROM THE START, which is the easy case, and the campaign says so.
#   2. THE PILOT CANNOT DISAGREE WITH HIS BRIEF, AND WHAT LOOKS LIKE A RECOVERY IS A DEAD-BAND ACCIDENT.
#      `FBMig29Pilot` types what it was given and has no path to re-enter a call it has reason to doubt.
#      `FBPilot`'s own uncued search law does keep posting an elevation, but only when ITS OWN wanted
#      angle has moved more than `kInterceptElDeadDeg` = 2.0 deg from ITS OWN last command - and that
#      cache is per aircraft. MEASURED in sortie 02: the wingman's cache sat at 0.0, drifted past the
#      band at t = 55.9 and pulled the antenna back down; the leader's sat at -2.0 from t = 3.5, never
#      drifted, and never looked at the raid again. One aircraft of two recovered, 28 s late, and not
#      because anybody doubted the controller. So 02 and 03 measure the cost of a wrong entry AND the
#      absence of any deliberate recovery, and the two cannot be separated inside one file.
#   3. THE GCI ELEVATION ENTRY IS A WORLD-FRAME ANGLE IN A BODY-FRAME COMMAND (doc/pilot.md 2.15, found
#      by O5 and STILL OPEN on the tree this campaign was flown against). Every interceptor in all ten
#      files is therefore laid out in LEVEL flight, and what that costs is measured in this campaign's
#      own attribution run rather than argued (see doc/campaigns/o2-pvo-intercept.md, State).
#   4. `FBMissionRunner` ends the whole run at the first flight-monitor K.O. (`FirstFlightKo`).
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: THE LOOP, TIMED. How many seconds from the controller's call to a firm
# track, and how much of that is the three typed entries? This is the only number the campaign
# contract demands of every mission, and this file is where it is established.
#
# THE GEOMETRY, and both halves are deliberate. (a) OFF-NOSE: the raid runs a CONSTANT-BEARING
# course at 250 deg while the barrier holds 270, so it sits 20 deg off the nose for the whole
# closure. That is what makes sortie 03 askable at all - the three ZONE sectors overlap and a
# target dead ahead is inside every one of them. (b) CO-ALTITUDE: it puts the correct scan
# elevation at -0.03 deg, so sortie 02's wrong altitude band is the only thing that moves it.
# Both jets are LEVEL, which disclosure 3 above says is not a convenience but a constraint.
#
# READING RULE (binding): the verdict is THE CHAIN AND ITS SECONDS, never the exit code, and exit 3
# is the expected shape. Read, in this order:
#   1. `gci BRAA` -> `gci ENTER_ELEV` -> `gci ENTER_ZONE` -> `gci RADAR_ILLUM` -> `n019 EMISSION`
#      -> `radar RADAR_CONTACT`: the loop, entry by entry, with its two intervals.
#   2. `rwr THREAT_NEW unit=p1int kind=fire-control`: the price of the last entry, measured on the
#      OTHER aircraft. `kind=surface-search` at t=0.1 is the P-18 and is not it.
#   3. `sms RELEASE`, `stores DETONATION ... missM` against the R-27R's 13.8 m fuze, and then
#      `damage SYSTEM` - and read the ZONE the warhead hit, because an intercept that connects is
#      not automatically an intercept that kills.
# exit 2 (CRASH) would be a real failure.
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-29, `--elev const`, standalone AND as campaign step 1 - identical, per-mission
# fingerprint 7b48d2816b676d16, exit 3): THE LOOP IS 11.0 SECONDS AND IT SPLITS 8.0 + 3.0.
#   gci BRAA t=19.9 -> ENTER_ELEV t=19.9 (elDeg -0.025) -> ENTER_ZONE t=21.9 (offDeg -20.05, zone=left)
#   -> RADAR_ILLUM t=23.9 -> n019 EMISSION t=27.9 -> radar RADAR_CONTACT t=30.9 at 16.08 nm (29.78 km).
#   CALL -> RADIATING 8.0 s (the three typed entries plus the emission command's own bus latency);
#   RADIATING -> FIRM TRACK 3.0 s (one N019 RAD frame); CALL -> TRACK 11.0 s. The 8.0 s reproduces
#   `mig29-intercept.fbm`'s figure on a different geometry, so it is a property of the entry chain and
#   not of that file.
# THE PRICE, ON THE OTHER AIRCRAFT: `rwr THREAT_NEW unit=p1int kind=fire-control` at t=28.0 - 0.1 s
#   after the emission. Before that the intruder hears only `kind=surface-search` (the P-18, from
#   t=0.1). The fighter's whole surprise is spent in one tenth of a second, by the third entry.
# AND AN INTERCEPT THAT CONNECTS IS NOT AN INTERCEPT THAT KILLS. Both R-27R away at t=45.9, both onto
#   the same intruder (the flight sort does not split - the identical artefact o1-02, o4-10 and o5-01
#   measured). Arrivals 4.85 m and 4.75 m against a 13.8 m fuze, both in the FORWARD zone: twelve
#   avionics systems failed, engine, flight controls and structure only DEGRADED, so `CombatEffective`
#   holds, `kill team friendly` reads UNMET and the intruder finishes its route at t=379.5 blind,
#   deaf and unarmed. That is the model, it is reported rather than tuned, and sortie 02 shows the
#   other face of the same lottery.
# THE KOLS is powered in every sortie of this campaign and its first contact here is t=95.0 - 64 s
#   AFTER the radar had the target. Head-on and cold, the passive channel is the slow one.

unit p1kna
  team hostile
  flight brk1 1
  module mig29
  spawn 47.30000 48.20000 8000 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_emission off              # POWER-UP POSITION BY DOCTRINE: this jet starts silent
  set rwr on
  set iff_interrogator on
  set kols_mode ir
  set brief_sort left
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  set brief_gci 20 250 38 8
  set brief_gci 50 250 25 8
  set brief_gci 80 250 12 8
  wp 47.30000 47.60000 8000 450      # the briefed vector: what Search flies while blind
  objective kill team friendly
  objective protect unit p1cp
  objective survive

unit p1knb
  team hostile
  flight brk1 2
  module mig29
  spawn 47.31200 48.21500 8150 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_emission off
  set rwr on
  set iff_interrogator on
  set kols_mode ir
  set brief_sort left
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  set brief_gci 20 250 38 8
  set brief_gci 50 250 25 8
  set brief_gci 80 250 12 8
  wp 47.30000 47.60000 8000 450
  objective kill team friendly
  objective protect unit p1cp
  objective survive

unit p1int
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 47.15500 47.61500 8000 50.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set fcr_mode off                   # it radiates NOTHING: every warning it gets came from the barrier
  set rwr on                         # the price meter
  set datalink off
  wp 47.67500 48.53000 8000 450      # running in on the defended complex

unit p1ews
  module p18
  team hostile
  spawn 47.55000 48.20000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free

unit p1cp
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 47.67500 48.53000 ground 0.0 0

unit p1veh
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 47.68500 48.52000 ground 0.0 0
